  m_Name: FrancisTurbineData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Francis Turbine
  engineDescription: "A Francis turbine is a reaction turbine that converts the hydraulic
    energy of water into mechanical energy. It is one of the most widely used turbines
    in hydroelectric power plants and is suitable for medium head (30\u2013300 m)
    and medium discharge conditions. The main components include the spiral casing,
    guide vanes (wicket gates), runner, shaft, and draft tube. During operation,
    water enters the spiral casing and is directed by the guide vanes onto the runner
    blades, causing the runner to rotate. The rotating shaft drives a generator to
    produce electricity, while the water exits through the draft tube. From an engineering
    perspective, understanding turbine efficiency, hydraulic head, flow rate, reaction
    principle, cavitation, specific speed, and governor control is essential for
    the design, operation, and maintenance of Francis turbines, ensuring efficient
    and reliable power generation.\r\n"
  engineCategory: Engineering
